# Trivy ignore policy for frankidugboe.com
#
# Auto-loaded by `trivy config` from the repo root (CI working directory).
# Each suppression is a deliberate decision documented in
# docs/security-policy.md and mirrored in .checkov.yaml.

# AWS-0011 (HIGH): CloudFront distribution does not have a WAF in front.
# False positive under static analysis. The distribution DOES attach a WAFv2
# Web ACL (module.waf -> cloudfront web_acl_id). Because the association is a
# cross-module variable reference rather than a literal, Trivy cannot resolve
# it statically. Mirrors Checkov CKV_AWS_68.
AWS-0011

# AWS-0132 (HIGH): S3 encryption should use Customer Managed Keys.
# Accepted risk. Both buckets use SSE-S3 (AES256). The origin bucket holds
# only public static assets and the Terraform state bucket holds no secrets,
# so a customer-managed KMS key adds key-management cost and complexity for
# no meaningful risk reduction here. Mirrors Checkov CKV_AWS_145.
AWS-0132

# AWS-0136 (HIGH): SNS topic encryption does not use a customer managed key.
# Accepted risk. The alerts topic carries only budget and CloudWatch alarm
# notifications (no sensitive data) and is encrypted with the AWS-managed SNS
# key. A customer-managed key adds cost/complexity for no meaningful gain here,
# consistent with the SSE-S3 decision (AWS-0132 / CKV_AWS_145).
AWS-0136
